@block DoublePendCtrl begin
    # pendulum-double-fixed controller: swing-up, catch and balance of the fixed-pivot chain, sampled at 1 kHz (D28 firmware).
    #
    # Generated by design/design.py: every number below is a constant table of that script.
    #
    #   t < t_on                    phase 0, u = 0 (hanging, motor voltage 0)
    #   t >= t_on, not caught       phase 1, time-varying LQR along the optimised trajectory
    #                                 u = u_ff(t - t_on) - K(t - t_on) (x - x_ref(t - t_on))
    #                               the tables hold one row every dt_tab = 10 ms; the row weights are the
    #                               hat functions of the position in the table, i.e. linear interpolation,
    #                               and the last row is held beyond the table
    #   V(x) < V_catch              catch: latched, phase 2, infinite-horizon LQR
    #                                 u = -K_lqr (x - x_up),  V(x) = (x - x_up)' P_lqr (x - x_up)
    #
    # x = [q1 .. qn, qd1 .. qdn] (q1 the absolute angle of link 1 from +x, q2.. relative joint angles),
    # x_up = [pi/2, 0, .., 0]. The output is the motor terminal voltage, clamped to +-u_max.
